IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc16-dna-definitions`

-- ccc16-tests-dna-definitions.l4 -- tests for ccc16-dna-definitions.l4 (section 487.04).
-- Every expected value was decided from the text of lines 9292-9543 before the run and is written beside its assertion.
-- A failing assertion is a finding; no expected value was edited to match the code.

§ `Fixtures`

-- an offence of this Act as it reads now, charged itself, for no particular purpose, indictable, maximum fourteen years
GIVEN sec IS A NUMBER
      sub IS A STRING
GIVETH A `s 487.04 facts of the offence`
`s 487.04 test: a provision of this Act` MEANS `s 487.04 facts of the offence` WITH
    `the provision that creates the offence` IS `Provision of the Code` OF sec, sub
    `where that provision is found` IS `s 487.04 this Act as it reads now`
    `how the person is charged` IS `s 487.04 with the listed offence itself`
    `the purpose` IS `s 487.04 another purpose`
    `the offence may be prosecuted by indictment` IS TRUE
    `the offence is prosecuted by indictment` IS TRUE
    `the maximum imprisonment for the offence` IS `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 14, 0, 0, FALSE)
    `the intent of an assault under subsection 246(1) is to commit an offence referred to in subparagraphs (b)(i) to (vi)` IS FALSE

-- a provision of another instrument or vintage, charged itself
GIVEN sec IS A NUMBER
      sub IS A STRING
      inst IS A `s 487.04 where the provision is found`
GIVETH A `s 487.04 facts of the offence`
`s 487.04 test: a provision found in` MEANS `s 487.04 facts of the offence` WITH
    `the provision that creates the offence` IS `Provision of the Code` OF sec, sub
    `where that provision is found` IS inst
    `how the person is charged` IS `s 487.04 with the listed offence itself`
    `the purpose` IS `s 487.04 another purpose`
    `the offence may be prosecuted by indictment` IS TRUE
    `the offence is prosecuted by indictment` IS TRUE
    `the maximum imprisonment for the offence` IS `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 14, 0, 0, FALSE)
    `the intent of an assault under subsection 246(1) is to commit an offence referred to in subparagraphs (b)(i) to (vi)` IS FALSE

-- an offence of this Act, charged as an attempt or a conspiracy, for a stated purpose
GIVEN sec IS A NUMBER
      sub IS A STRING
      how IS A `s 487.04 how the person is charged`
      purpose IS A `s 487.04 the purpose the answer is wanted for`
GIVETH A `s 487.04 facts of the offence`
`s 487.04 test: a provision of this Act charged as` MEANS `s 487.04 facts of the offence` WITH
    `the provision that creates the offence` IS `Provision of the Code` OF sec, sub
    `where that provision is found` IS `s 487.04 this Act as it reads now`
    `how the person is charged` IS how
    `the purpose` IS purpose
    `the offence may be prosecuted by indictment` IS TRUE
    `the offence is prosecuted by indictment` IS TRUE
    `the maximum imprisonment for the offence` IS `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 14, 0, 0, FALSE)
    `the intent of an assault under subsection 246(1) is to commit an offence referred to in subparagraphs (b)(i) to (vi)` IS FALSE

-- an offence of this Act prosecuted in a stated way, with a stated maximum, for a stated purpose
GIVEN sec IS A NUMBER
      sub IS A STRING
      purpose IS A `s 487.04 the purpose the answer is wanted for`
      may IS A BOOLEAN
      prosecuted IS A BOOLEAN
      max IS AN Imprisonment
GIVETH A `s 487.04 facts of the offence`
`s 487.04 test: a prosecution of a provision of this Act` MEANS `s 487.04 facts of the offence` WITH
    `the provision that creates the offence` IS `Provision of the Code` OF sec, sub
    `where that provision is found` IS `s 487.04 this Act as it reads now`
    `how the person is charged` IS `s 487.04 with the listed offence itself`
    `the purpose` IS purpose
    `the offence may be prosecuted by indictment` IS may
    `the offence is prosecuted by indictment` IS prosecuted
    `the maximum imprisonment for the offence` IS max
    `the intent of an assault under subsection 246(1) is to commit an offence referred to in subparagraphs (b)(i) to (vi)` IS FALSE

-- a provision of another instrument or vintage, charged in a stated way for a stated purpose
GIVEN sec IS A NUMBER
      sub IS A STRING
      inst IS A `s 487.04 where the provision is found`
      how IS A `s 487.04 how the person is charged`
      purpose IS A `s 487.04 the purpose the answer is wanted for`
GIVETH A `s 487.04 facts of the offence`
`s 487.04 test: a provision found in, charged as` MEANS `s 487.04 facts of the offence` WITH
    `the provision that creates the offence` IS `Provision of the Code` OF sec, sub
    `where that provision is found` IS inst
    `how the person is charged` IS how
    `the purpose` IS purpose
    `the offence may be prosecuted by indictment` IS TRUE
    `the offence is prosecuted by indictment` IS TRUE
    `the maximum imprisonment for the offence` IS `imprisonment for life`
    `the intent of an assault under subsection 246(1) is to commit an offence referred to in subparagraphs (b)(i) to (vi)` IS FALSE

-- the 1970 Criminal Code, subsection 246(1), with the intent fact stated
GIVEN intent IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 487.04 facts of the offence`
`s 487.04 test: assault with intent under the 1970 Code` MEANS `s 487.04 facts of the offence` WITH
    `the provision that creates the offence` IS `Provision of the Code` OF 246, "(1)"
    `where that provision is found` IS `s 487.04 the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as it read from time to time before January 4, 1983`
    `how the person is charged` IS `s 487.04 with the listed offence itself`
    `the purpose` IS `s 487.04 another purpose`
    `the offence may be prosecuted by indictment` IS TRUE
    `the offence is prosecuted by indictment` IS TRUE
    `the maximum imprisonment for the offence` IS `imprisonment for life`
    `the intent of an assault under subsection 246(1) is to commit an offence referred to in subparagraphs (b)(i) to (vi)` IS intent

`s 487.04 test: the 1970 Code before 1983` MEANS `s 487.04 the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as it read from time to time before January 4, 1983`
`s 487.04 test: the 1970 Code before 1988` MEANS `s 487.04 the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as it read from time to time before January 1, 1988`
`s 487.04 test: the 1970 Code as enacted by chapter 125` MEANS `s 487.04 the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as enacted by section 19 of chapter 125 of the Statutes of Canada, 1980-81-82-83`
`s 487.04 test: this Act before the paragraph's day` MEANS `s 487.04 this Act as it read from time to time before the day on which the paragraph that names it comes into force`
`s 487.04 test: this Act before the conveyances Act` MEANS `s 487.04 this Act as it read from time to time before the day on which section 14 of the Act to amend the Criminal Code (offences relating to conveyances) comes into force`

§ `s 487.04 -- the scope of the definitions (line 9292)`

-- "In this section and in sections 487.05 to 487.0911": 487.04 and 487.05 to 487.0911 inside; 487.03 and 487.1 outside (a limit by its own wording: NOTHING).
#ASSERT `s 487.04 the definitions apply in the section` 487.04 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.04 the definitions apply in the section` 487.05 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.04 the definitions apply in the section` 487.051 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.04 the definitions apply in the section` 487.0911 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.04 the definitions apply in the section` 487.03 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.04 the definitions apply in the section` 487.049 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.04 the definitions apply in the section` 487.1 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 487.04 -- adult, DNA, young person, provincial court judge, Young Offenders Act`

#ASSERT `s 487.04 adult` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.04 adult` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 487.04 adult` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- the meaning is the Youth Criminal Justice Act's: not among the sources

#ASSERT `s 487.04 DNA` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.04 DNA` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "DNA means deoxyribonucleic acid"

-- young person: "as the case may be" -- the Act the caller names answers; if the text does not say which, NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 487.04 young person` `s 487.04 the Youth Criminal Justice Act` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.04 young person` `s 487.04 the Youth Criminal Justice Act` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 487.04 young person` `s 487.04 the Young Offenders Act` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.04 young person` `s 487.04 the Young Offenders Act` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 487.04 young person` `s 487.04 the text does not say which of the two Acts applies` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.04 young person` `s 487.04 the Youth Criminal Justice Act` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- provincial court judge, in relation to a young person, "includes" a youth justice court judge: a listed case; anything else is not covered.
#ASSERT `s 487.04 provincial court judge, in relation to a young person, includes a youth justice court judge` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.04 provincial court judge, in relation to a young person, includes a youth justice court judge` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.04 provincial court judge, in relation to a young person, includes a youth justice court judge` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 487.04 Young Offenders Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.04 Young Offenders Act` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "means chapter Y-1 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1985"

§ `s 487.04 -- forensic DNA analysis`

-- (a) a substance taken in execution of a warrant under section 487.05: analysis, comparison with the 487.05(1)(b) substance, and incidental tests.
#ASSERT `s 487.04 forensic DNA analysis` `s 487.04 taken from a person in execution of a warrant under section 487.05` EQUALS JUST `s 487.04 analysis of the substance, comparison of the results with the results of the analysis of the DNA in the substance referred to in paragraph 487.05(1)(b), and any incidental tests associated with that analysis`
-- (b) the four other kinds: analysis of the bodily substance only.
#ASSERT `s 487.04 forensic DNA analysis` `s 487.04 provided voluntarily in the course of an investigation of a designated offence` EQUALS JUST `s 487.04 analysis of the bodily substance`
#ASSERT `s 487.04 forensic DNA analysis` `s 487.04 taken from a person under an order made under section 487.051` EQUALS JUST `s 487.04 analysis of the bodily substance`
#ASSERT `s 487.04 forensic DNA analysis` `s 487.04 taken from a person under an authorization granted under section 487.055 or 487.091` EQUALS JUST `s 487.04 analysis of the bodily substance`
#ASSERT `s 487.04 forensic DNA analysis` `s 487.04 a bodily substance referred to in paragraph 487.05(1)(b)` EQUALS JUST `s 487.04 analysis of the bodily substance`
-- a substance that came to be analysed another way: neither paragraph speaks to it.
#ASSERT `s 487.04 forensic DNA analysis` `s 487.04 a bodily substance that came to be analysed in some other way` EQUALS NOTHING

